WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0091: the storeys above the character are not drawn while she is below them.

The design rule: what stands between the camera and the character is handled
three ways depending on what it is: ceilings, bushes, skinny trees and posts **phase out**; walls get
the **see-through opening** 0090 cuts; mountains, rocks and big trees the camera **bumps into**. And
on floors, like BG3: "while on the first floor the second floor should just be fully faded out, and
then come back when you do go upstairs".

This is the first of the three: a ceiling, and every storey above her, goes. WoW's buildings are
already grouped (a roof, a floor, a room are separate MOGP groups with their own bounds), so the
piece to take is the group, and `GxSel::drawn` already decides that per frame per group.

- wmo_portal: while the see-through is live, the indoor groups (MOGP `0x2000`) her chest is in, as
  one world box per placement (every corner through the placement's transform, so a rotated
  building's box is right), into the `SeeRooms` resource. None when she is in no indoor group.
- static_gx/cull.rs: a group of that placement whose box lies entirely above her head and over that
  room's footprint (grown 2 yd) is not drawn. Her own floor and the stairs reach down to her and
  stay; walking past a house never opens it; a city WMO (Orgrimmar is one) loses only what is above
  the room she is in, never a tower across the city. The props of those groups go with them (a prop
  set whose referring rooms are all gone): a bed left floating where the floor was is not a storey
  gone. So do the units standing on them (wmo_portal's `hide_units_above_her`, after the exterior
  election, so they are back the frame she climbs up): the NPC upstairs no longer floats.

History, so nobody walks it again: the first build had no height test and took the floor and the
far walls with the roof, leaving her on a scrap of plank in open sky; a "does the box contain her,
give or take 1.5 yd" test kept every low ceiling; a version that also asked the group to cross the
line from the eye to her left half the upstairs standing round her (the bed, the far walls), which
is not what BG3 does.

It pays off with the plugin's `free` eye clearance (`WOWBG3_CAM_INDOOR`, the default), which lets the
camera rise to BG3's own zoom indoors instead of pinning it under the ceiling.

The storey does not pop: it fades out and back in with BG3's own per-object fade, the sixteen-step
dissolve over the 4x4 Bayer table BG3 writes into its stencil every frame (`FadePatternOnePass.bshd`,
`M[x%4][y%4] < k`), at BG3's own speed (`FadeOutSpeed` 5.0, the value on most objects that set one:
a fifth of a second). cull.rs keeps each group's fade and walks it every frame; the level (0 to 16)
rides in bits 15..19 of the item records' flags column (render.rs, synced like the fog bit), and
static_gx.wgsl discards by it; a group fully faded is not drawn at all, and a prop set fades with the
least faded of its rooms. The units standing up there are hidden and shown at once (their bodies are
not static_gx draws).

Not in this patch: the same treatment for bushes, skinny trees and posts, which are static_gx items rather
than WMO groups; and big doodads (rocks, big trees) in the plugin's camera bump, which in `free`
bumps into terrain only.

